00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:36.200
to undo all the resource
creation that it applied.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.850
So if you're ready, Martin,
if you want to type terraform

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:41.380
destroy.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:42.880
MARTIN OMANDER: Oh, my gosh.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:45.250
terraform destroy.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:46.210
Like so?

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:47.290
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: Yep.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:50.882
And you're going to have to
enter in your project, as well.

00:10:50.882 --> 00:10:51.840
MARTIN OMANDER: Ah, OK.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:54.090
Should we do this--

00:10:54.090 --> 00:11:00.510
whoops-- -var project=--

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:01.170
there it is.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.050
All right.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:02.690
Let's do it.

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:13.350
18 things will be destroyed.

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:14.485
Oh, my gosh.

00:11:14.485 --> 00:11:16.110
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: We
created 18 things,

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:17.740
now we're going to
destroy 18 things.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.820
So if you're ready, Martin,
Y-E-S, and Terraform

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:24.092
will remove everything
that it created.

00:11:24.092 --> 00:11:25.050
MARTIN OMANDER: Oh, my.

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:39.890
All right, so it's destroyed.

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:43.520
Now if I hit this, the
application of the web page--

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:44.120
oh, my gosh.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:45.650
It's not even I have no cats.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:47.270
It's literally a 404.

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.940
The URL doesn't exist, eh?

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:53.510
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: We
destroyed everything.

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:55.160
MARTIN OMANDER: Wow, OK.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.780
How do I get it back?

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:59.015
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN:
terraform apply.

00:11:59.015 --> 00:12:00.140
MARTIN OMANDER: Oh, really?

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:01.580
OK, let's do that.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:07.920
All right.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:10.380
18 things will be
added, it says.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:11.580
OK, let's do it.

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:14.930
All right.

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:17.390
The terraform apply is all done.

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:20.120
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: Yeah, and
your cats should now be back.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.578
MARTIN OMANDER:
Oh, let's see here.

00:12:21.578 --> 00:12:24.230
So, OK, before, I
got a 404 error,

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:28.270
because the service
had been removed.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:29.830
Ah, the cats are back.

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:30.700
I'm relieved.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.440
That was really cool, Katie.

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:34.315
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: Did
you want to take a look

00:12:34.315 --> 00:12:38.570
at what the Terraform manifests
look like, while we're here?

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:39.850
MARTIN OMANDER: Ah, yes.

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:42.130
What's the magic that
makes all of this happen?

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:44.463
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: No magic,
just the careful application

00:12:44.463 --> 00:12:47.475
of configuration files.

00:12:47.475 --> 00:12:49.700
MARTIN OMANDER:
[LAUGHS] Very good.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:50.450
Let's have a look.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.075
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN:
You can go to GitHub,

00:12:52.075 --> 00:12:56.040
or we can use the
Cloud Shell Editor.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:59.820
MARTIN OMANDER: All right,
I'm going to GitHub.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:03.970
I'll go up in the
directory here.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:08.190
Ah, .tf-- does that have
anything to do with it?

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:11.220
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: Yep, .tf
is for Terraform manifest.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.960
So there are a couple
of manifests in here.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:17.400
The three main ones that are
standard names for Terraform

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:22.210
manifests are the main, which
is the main file, variables

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:25.950
for variables, and then
outputs for outputs.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.540
Each of the other
manifests that I

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:29.830
have there for
this demonstration

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.785
are just a logical
separation of each

00:13:31.785 --> 00:13:34.160
of the different components--
the function for functions,

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.680
the service for service,
media for media, et cetera.

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:39.180
Those folders that
I've got in there

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:41.620
are also just the source code.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.230
So if you have a
look at the function,

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:46.950
you'll end up with
the requirements.txt

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:51.360
and the application file that we
saw earlier in Cloud Functions.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:52.800
So that's just
the function code.

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.103
Same for the service code.

00:13:55.103 --> 00:13:57.103
But it's those Terraform
manifests that define--

00:13:57.103 --> 00:13:59.478
MARTIN OMANDER: Ah, the service
is the Cloud Run service?

00:13:59.478 --> 00:14:00.460
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: Yeah.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:01.860
Yeah.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.420
MARTIN OMANDER: Aha.

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:05.010
Cool.

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:06.760
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: But
it's those manifests

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:11.587
that define what we want
our project state to be.

00:14:11.587 --> 00:14:12.670
MARTIN OMANDER: Oh, I see.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:14.530
They list the services,
and the buckets,

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:16.930
and everything that's
in these .tf files.

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:18.730
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: Yeah.

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:20.260
MARTIN OMANDER: Cool.

00:14:20.260 --> 00:14:23.050
So, Katie, I have one
more question for you.

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:24.940
When I was running
this terraform apply,

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:28.840
it always asked me
to input yes, Y-E-S,

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.130
to actually make it happen.

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:32.510
Can I automate
that away, as well?

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:34.540
KATIE MCLAUGHLIN: Yes, but.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.040
You can automate it away.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:40.090
You can auto-approve, but
when you are running Terraform

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:43.060
locally, you really should be
checking what you're doing.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:49.100
For automation pipelines
and continuous deployment,

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:51.520
you can't have a
human type Y-E-S.

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:53.210
So there are ways
Terraform can do that.

00:14:53.210 --> 00:14:55.630
But when you're learning,
make sure that you actually

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:58.160
go back and read what Terraform
is going to do, especially

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.160
if you start destroying
stuff, just to make sure

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.720
that you're in
the right project,

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:05.718
that you're manipulating the
resources that you expect.

00:15:05.718 --> 00:15:06.760
MARTIN OMANDER: Ah, cool.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:07.690
Got it.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:11.200
Well, I can't wait to write
